\newlabel{sec:restoration}{{4.1}{4}{Coordinate restoration helps, but pooled response recovery is limited}{subsection.4.1}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Restoration quality and supervision tradeoffs. A--B: all eight families and both objectives, as hierarchical means over 14 people and three seeds, pooled over estimators. Circles use coordinate supervision; open triangles add scalar and geometry terms. Direct fitting adapts its encoder; all other encoders are frozen. Zero response (5.81$^{\circ }$) appears only in A. C: paired change-minus-coordinate waveform effects with crossed-person/seed 95\% intervals (2,000 draws), newly computed and exploratory; positive values indicate deterioration. Responses and waveforms retain failures at 720$^{\circ }$ and 180$^{\circ }$, respectively. Families share the development cohort and are not independent replications.}}{5}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:restoration}{{2}{5}{Restoration quality and supervision tradeoffs. A--B: all eight families and both objectives, as hierarchical means over 14 people and three seeds, pooled over estimators. Circles use coordinate supervision; open triangles add scalar and geometry terms. Direct fitting adapts its encoder; all other encoders are frozen. Zero response (5.81$\dg $) appears only in A. C: paired change-minus-coordinate waveform effects with crossed-person/seed 95\% intervals (2,000 draws), newly computed and exploratory; positive values indicate deterioration. Responses and waveforms retain failures at 720$\dg $ and 180$\dg $, respectively. Families share the development cohort and are not independent replications}{figure.2}{}}
